# ---- Third-party resources (downloaded, not authored) ----
# `server.cfg.example` ensures all of these at startup. They are EXTERNAL
# dependencies: download them, do not vendor them. Tracking them would put
# someone else's repository into this one's history, tie us to their release
# cadence, and bury our own diff under theirs.
#
# `/resources/[nifty]` is OUR code and stays tracked — the bracket is literal
# gitignore syntax, so it must not be repeated here.
# One of these was already committed by accident; the follow-up commit removes
# them again. Verified with `git ls-tree -r HEAD~1 resources/`.
/resources/oxmysql/
/resources/bob74_ipl*/
/resources/mapmanager/
/resources/spawnmanager/
/resources/sessionmanager/
/resources/chat/
/resources/[map]/

# ---- Local test artefacts ----
*.sql.bak
/tmp/
*.local.*